Source code
-----------
The complete corresponding source of every image published as
ghcr.io/<owner>/docker-seedbox-{api,web,gateway,vpn,qbittorrent} is the Git repository
https://github.com/ma-04/docker-seedbox at the tag that names the image version (for example
v1.2.3 for :1.2.3; :edge is the head of the main branch at build time). Each image carries the label
org.opencontainers.image.source pointing at that repository and org.opencontainers.image.revision with the commit.
Build instructions: README.md and docs/deployment.md ("./setup.sh --build").

If you run a modified version of docker-seedbox as a network service, AGPL-3.0 section 13 requires that you offer
its users the corresponding source of your modified version.

Third-party software
--------------------
The container images redistribute or are built on third-party software that keeps its own licenses. They are listed,
with where to get their source, in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. Nothing in this repository changes those licenses.
The qbittorrent image is the unmodified official qBittorrent-nox image (GPL-2.0-or-later) plus one shell script
(services/qbittorrent/seed-config.sh, AGPL-3.0-only); the vpn image bundles the GPL-2.0 wireguard-tools and nftables
as separate programs that are executed, not linked.

